          "content": {
            "id": "b6c3e474-be47-3abd-ad99-f7a2a15aaad5",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Mortgage rates inch lower, Nvidia & Broadcom boosted by TSM",
            "description": "<p>Yahoo Finance anchor <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/julie-hyman/\">Julie Hyman</a> tracks Thursday's top moving stocks and biggest market stories in this<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-minute/\"> Market Minute</a>.</p>\n<p>Mortgage rates are slightly lower this week, with the 30-year fixed rate down to 6.27% from 6.3%, according to data from Freddie Mac (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/FMCC\">FMCC</a>).</p>\n<p>Chip stocks, including Nvidia (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/NVDA\">NVDA</a>), Broadcom (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AVGO\">AVGO</a>), and Arm Holdings (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/ARM\">ARM</a>), are jumping after Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:7;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/TSM\">TSM</a>) delivered on third quarter earnings results.</p>\n<p>American Battery Technology Company (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:8;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/ABAT\">ABAT</a>) stock is sinking after the company announced that the US Department of Energy (DOE) canceled its grant funding.</p>\n<p>Stay up to date on the latest market action, minute-by-minute, with <a data-i13n=\"cpos:9;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-minute/\">Yahoo Finance's Market Minute.</a></p>",
            "summary": "Yahoo Finance anchor Julie Hyman tracks Thursday's top moving stocks and biggest market stories in this Market Minute. Mortgage rates are slightly lower this week, with the 30-year fixed rate down to 6.27% from 6.3%, according to data from Freddie Mac (FMCC). Chip stocks, including Nvidia (NVDA), Broadcom (AVGO), and Arm Holdings (ARM), are jumping after Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company (TSM) delivered on third quarter earnings results. American Battery Technology Company (ABAT) stock is sinking after the company announced that the US Department of Energy (DOE) canceled its grant funding. Stay up to date on the latest market action, minute-by-minute, with Yahoo Finance's Market Minute.",
